<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>iOS UIKit Course</title><link>/docs/6.-functions/</link><description>Recent content on iOS UIKit Course</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="/docs/6.-functions/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>6.1. Writing functions</title><link>/docs/6.-functions/6.1.-writing-functions/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/docs/6.-functions/6.1.-writing-functions/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="61-writing-functions"&gt;6.1. Writing functions&lt;a class="anchor" href="#61-writing-functions"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To write a function in Swift, we use the keyword &lt;code&gt;func&lt;/code&gt; followed by the function&amp;rsquo;s name, parameter list, return data type, and body (the code block). A general structure of a Swift function is:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;func functionName(parameter1:DataType, parameter2:DataType, ...) -&amp;gt; ReturnDataType{
 //code block
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;h3 id="simple-functions"&gt;Simple functions&lt;a class="anchor" href="#simple-functions"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For a function, the list of parameters can be empty, meaning if our function does not require any data from us to run, we do not need to define any parameters. For example, a function to print &amp;ldquo;Hello World&amp;rdquo; could be:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>6.2. Functions with parameters</title><link>/docs/6.-functions/6.2.-functions-with-parameters/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/docs/6.-functions/6.2.-functions-with-parameters/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="62-functions-with-parameters"&gt;6.2. Functions with parameters&lt;a class="anchor" href="#62-functions-with-parameters"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Now, let&amp;rsquo;s write a function that accepts parameters and do some tasks. The following code accepts the name and age of a person as parameters and prints the details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-swift" data-lang="swift"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;//function definition...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;func&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;printDetails&lt;/span&gt;(name:String, age:Int){
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; print(
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt; The user&amp;#39;s name is: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;\(&lt;/span&gt;name&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt; The user&amp;#39;s age is: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;\(&lt;/span&gt;age&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;\(&lt;/span&gt;name&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt; is awesome!
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt; &amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; )
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;//calling the function...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;printDetails(name: &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;Donald&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, age: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;25&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;It prints:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;The user&amp;#39;s name is: Donald.
The user&amp;#39;s age is: 25.
Donald is awesome!&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</description></item><item><title>6.3. Functions that return a value</title><link>/docs/6.-functions/6.3.-functions-that-return-a-value/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/docs/6.-functions/6.3.-functions-that-return-a-value/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="63-functions-that-return-a-value"&gt;6.3. Functions that return a value&lt;a class="anchor" href="#63-functions-that-return-a-value"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Now, let&amp;rsquo;s think about a function that accepts an array of integers as a parameter and returns the sum of the integers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-swift" data-lang="swift"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;func&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;sumOf&lt;/span&gt;(array:[Int]) -&amp;gt; Int{
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; sum = &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; item &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; array{
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; sum &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;+=&lt;/span&gt; item
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; }
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; 
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;//returns the value...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; sum
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;//calling the function with an integer array&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;print(sumOf(array: [&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;]))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;It prints:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;15&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;You can get the returned value and store it to a constant or variable:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>6.4. More on function parameters</title><link>/docs/6.-functions/6.4.-more-on-function-parameters/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/docs/6.-functions/6.4.-more-on-function-parameters/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="64-more-on-function-parameters"&gt;6.4. More on function parameters&lt;a class="anchor" href="#64-more-on-function-parameters"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2 id="parameter-labels"&gt;Parameter labels&lt;a class="anchor" href="#parameter-labels"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Swift functions have the ability to have completely separate internal and external parameter names. Instead of having a single parameter name, the function below has two. The first one, &lt;code&gt;with&lt;/code&gt; is an external parameter name, which is the name that will refer to the parameter when we call the function. The second one, &lt;code&gt;vehicle&lt;/code&gt; is the internal parameter name which is the name we’ll use when we need to use the parameter within the function.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>6.5. Reference Code</title><link>/docs/6.-functions/6.5.-reference-code/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/docs/6.-functions/6.5.-reference-code/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="65-reference-code"&gt;6.5. Reference Code&lt;a class="anchor" href="#65-reference-code"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
